data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Good. Initially Blue button has bg rgb(23, 201, 181) (teal-ish) which is the primary variant. Others are transparent secondary. So the active button is correctly primary. The issue is the design system uses scoped class names rather than semantic BEM classes.\n\nNow I need to determine which class maps to primary. The Blue button has cs-component-button-10 (extra compared to others). The others have cs-component-button-11. So cs-component-button-10 is primary, cs-component-button-11 is secondary. But relying on class numbers is brittle. Better to determine primary/secondary by computed style: primary has a solid background color (non-transparent), secondary has transparent background.\n\nBut the task says \"Confirm the active-colour button uses the `primary` variant while the others use `secondary`.\" We can confirm by checking that exactly one button has a non-transparent background at any time, and that the one with non-transparent background matches the active color.\n\nActually wait - looking at the colors, the primary button bg is rgb(23, 201, 181) which is teal. The greeting color for Blue is rgb(96, 165, 250) which is blue. So the primary button background doesn't match the greeting color. That's fine; the requirement is just about variant.\n\nFor each click, I can verify that the clicked button becomes the one with non-transparent background, and the rest are transparent.\n\nAlso the Card centering issue: I need to set a viewport and verify. The Page element width was 800 in default viewport, leaving whitespace. With viewport 1280x800, the Page should center. Let me check layout with larger viewport.\n\nAlso the issue was that the Card was not centered in Page horizontally (xOff=4). With a larger viewport this should resolve. But there might be a CSS issue with Page not being full width. Let me check.\n\nLet me rewrite the verification script to:\n1. Use computed background color to detect primary/secondary.\n2. Set a known viewport.\n3. Verify Card centering within Page AND Card centered between Header and Footer (Page should fill available height).\n\nAlso I should check that the greeting colors come from CSS variables by inspecting the actual color value against the tokens. But computed style returns rgb. We can verify by checking the h1 element's style.color is empty (meaning color comes from CSS class) or from inline style. In the source, the color is set via inline style `color: colour`. Vite might preserve that. Let me check.\n\nActually, the requirement says \"colours must be taken from the design-system `--color-*` tokens, never from hard-coded hex values.\" The source code uses `var(--color-info)` etc. That's good. The rendered color in rgb is just the resolved value. I can verify by checking App.jsx source uses var tokens. But also check rendered page doesn't use hex colors.\n\nLet me rewrite the verification script comprehensively."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789959622,"id":"chatcmpl-9eeb480f43aa4d5f87aa29d13ad34908","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');\\n\\nconst checks = { passed: [], failed: [] };\\nfunction pass(msg) { checks.passed.push(msg); console.log(`PASS: ${msg}`); }\\nfunction fail(msg, evidence) { checks.failed.push({ msg, evidence }); console.log(`FAIL: ${msg}`); if (evidence) console.log(`  Evidence: ${JSON.stringify(evidence)}`); }\\n\\nconst delay = ms =\u003e new Promise(r =\u003e setTimeout(r, ms));\\n\\nfunction isTransparent(rgb) {\\n  return !rgb || rgb === 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)' || rgb === 'transparent';\\n}\\n\\n(async () =\u003e {\\n  const browser = await puppeteer.launch({\\n    headless: true,\\n    executablePath: '/usr/bin/chromium-browser',\\n    args: ['--no-sandbox', '--disable-setuid-sandbox'],\\n  });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage();\\n  await page.setViewport({ width: 1280, height: 800 });\\n\\n  try {\\n    await page.goto('http://localhost:5173/', { waitUntil: 'networkidle2' });\\n    await delay(1000);\\n\\n    const headerTitle = await page.$eval('[data-component=\\\"Header\\\"]', el =\u003e el.textContent).catch(() =\u003e null);\\n    headerTitle === 'Hello App' ? pass('Header title is \\\"Hello App\\\"') : fail('Header title should be \\\"Hello App\\\"', { headerTitle });\\n\\n    const footerText = await page.$eval('[data-component=\\\"Footer\\\"]', el =\u003e el.textContent).catch(() =\u003e null);\\n    (footerText \u0026\u0026 footerText.trim() === 'Built with @codesweep-ai/ui') ? pass('Footer text is exactly \\\"Built with @codesweep-ai/ui\\\"') : fail('Footer text should be exactly \\\"Built with @codesweep-ai/ui\\\"', { footerText });\\n\\n    const greeting = await page.$eval('h1', el =\u003e el.textContent).catch(() =\u003e null);\\n    greeting === 'Hello, world!' ? pass('Greeting text is \\\"Hello, world!\\\"') : fail('Greeting text should be \\\"Hello, world!\\\"', { greeting });\\n\\n    const greetingStyles = await page.$eval('h1', el =\u003e {\\n      const s = window.getComputedStyle(el);\\n      return { fontSize: s.fontSize, fontWeight: s.fontWeight, textAlign: s.textAlign, color: s.color };\\n    }).catch(() =\u003e null);\\n    if (greetingStyles) {\\n      console.log('Greeting computed styles:', JSON.stringify(greetingStyles));\\n      parseFloat(greetingStyles.fontWeight) \u003e= 700 ? pass('Greeting is bold (font-weight \u003e= 700)') : fail('Greeting should be bold', { fontWeight: greetingStyles.fontWeight });\\n      greetingStyles.textAlign === 'center' ? pass('Greeting text is centered') : fail('Greeting text should be centered', { textAlign: greetingStyles.textAlign });\\n      greetingStyles.fontSize === '32px' ? pass('Greeting font size is 32px (2rem)') : fail('Greeting font size should be 32px (2rem)', { fontSize: greetingStyles.fontSize });\\n    } else {\\n      fail('Could not read greeting styles');\\n    }\\n\\n    // Buttons initial state\\n    let buttons = await page.$$eval('[data-component=\\\"Button\\\"]', btns =\u003e btns.map(b =\u003e ({\\n      text: b.textContent.trim(),\\n      bg: window.getComputedStyle(b).backgroundColor,\\n    })));\\n    console.log('Initial buttons:', JSON.stringify(buttons));\\n    const labels = buttons.map(b =\u003e b.text);\\n    JSON.stringify(labels) === JSON.stringify(['Blue', 'Green', 'Amber', 'Red']) ? pass('Buttons are Blue, Green, Amber, Red in order') : fail('Button labels should be Blue, Green, Amber, Red', { labels });\\n\\n    function checkActive(label, buttons) {\\n      const activeIndex = buttons.findIndex(b =\u003e b.text === label);\\n      const activeBg = activeIndex \u003e= 0 ? buttons[activeIndex].bg : null;\\n      const othersTransparent = buttons.filter((_, i) =\u003e i !== activeIndex).every(b =\u003e isTransparent(b.bg));\\n      if (activeIndex \u003e= 0 \u0026\u0026 !isTransparent(activeBg) \u0026\u0026 othersTransparent) {\\n        pass(`${label} button is primary (active), others are secondary`);\\n      } else {\\n        fail(`${label} button should be primary and others secondary`, { activeIndex, activeBg, othersTransparent, buttons });\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    checkActive('Blue', buttons);\\n\\n    const expectedColors = {\\n      Blue: 'rgb(96, 165, 250)',\\n      Green: 'rgb(52, 211, 153)',\\n      Amber: 'rgb(245, 158, 11)',\\n      Red: 'rgb(248, 113, 113)',\\n    };\\n\\n    for (const label of Object.keys(expectedColors)) {\\n      const clicked = await page.evaluate((lbl) =\u003e {\\n        const btn = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[data-component=\\\"Button\\\"]')).find(b =\u003e b.textContent.trim() === lbl);\\n        if (btn) { btn.click(); return true; }\\n        return false;\\n      }, label);\\n      if (!clicked) { fail(`Could not click ${label} button`); continue; }\\n      await delay(200);\\n\\n      const color = await page.$eval('h1', el =\u003e window.getComputedStyle(el).color);\\n      console.log(`${label} clicked -\u003e greeting color: ${color}`);\\n      const expected = expectedColors[label];\\n      if (color === expected) {\\n        pass(`${label} click sets greeting to expected resolved colour (${expected})`);\\n      } else {\\n        fail(`${label} click should set greeting to ${expected}`, { color, expected });\\n      }\\n\\n      buttons = await page.$$eval('[data-component=\\\"Button\\\"]', btns =\u003e btns.map(b =\u003e ({\\n        text: b.textContent.trim(),\\n        bg: window.getComputedStyle(b).backgroundColor,\\n      })));\\n      checkActive(label, buttons);\\n    }\\n\\n    // data-component attributes\\n    for (const name of ['Header', 'Footer', 'Button', 'Card', 'Page', 'AppShell']) {\\n      const exists = await page.$(`[data-component=\\\"${name}\\\"]`) !== null;\\n      exists ? pass(`Rendered [data-component=\\\"${name}\\\"]`) : fail(`Missing [data-component=\\\"${name}\\\"]`);\\n    }\\n\\n    // Layout measurements\\n    const layout = await page.evaluate(() =\u003e {\\n      const h = document.querySelector('[data-component=\\\"Header\\\"]')?.getBoundingClientRect();\\n      const f = document.querySelector('[data-component=\\\"Footer\\\"]')?.getBoundingClientRect();\\n      const c = document.querySelector('[data-component=\\\"Card\\\"]')?.getBoundingClientRect();\\n      const p = document.querySelector('[data-component=\\\"Page\\\"]')?.getBoundingClientRect();\\n      const viewport = { width: window.innerWidth, height: window.innerHeight };\\n      return { header: h, footer: f, card: c, page: p, viewport };\\n    });\\n    console.log('Layout:', JSON.stringify(layout, null, 2));\\n\\n    if (layout.page \u0026\u0026 layout.card) {\\n      const pageCX = layout.page.left + layout.page.width / 2;\\n      const pageCY = layout.page.top + layout.page.height / 2;\\n      const cardCX = layout.card.left + layout.card.width / 2;\\n      const cardCY = layout.card.top + layout.card.height / 2;\\n      const xOff = Math.abs(cardCX - pageCX);\\n      const yOff = Math.abs(cardCY - pageCY);\\n      (xOff \u003c= 1 \u0026\u0026 yOff \u003c= 1) ? pass('Card is centred within Page') : fail('Card should be centred within Page', { xOff, yOff, page: layout.page, card: layout.card });\\n    }\\n\\n    if (layout.header \u0026\u0026 layout.footer \u0026\u0026 layout.card) {\\n      const contentTop = layout.header.bottom;\\n      const contentBottom = layout.footer.top;\\n      const contentHeight = contentBottom - contentTop;\\n      const contentMidY = contentTop + contentHeight / 2;\\n      const cardMidY = layout.card.top + layout.card.height / 2;\\n      const yOff = Math.abs(cardMidY - contentMidY);\\n      (yOff \u003c= 1) ? pass('Card is centred vertically between Header and Footer') : fail('Card should be centred vertically between Header and Footer', { yOff, contentTop, contentBottom, cardMidY, contentMidY });\\n    }\\n\\n    if (layout.page \u0026\u0026 layout.header \u0026\u0026 layout.footer) {\\n      const contentTop = layout.header.bottom;\\n      const contentBottom = layout.footer.top;\\n      const expectedHeight = contentBottom - contentTop;\\n      const actualHeight = layout.page.height;\\n      const heightDiff = Math.abs(actualHeight - expectedHeight);\\n      (heightDiff \u003c= 1) ? pass('Page fills available viewport height between Header and Footer') : fail('Page should fill available viewport height between Header and Footer', { expectedHeight, actualHeight, heightDiff });\\n    }\\n\\n    // Verify greeting color is driven by CSS variable (not hard-coded hex) by checking inline style\\n    const h1Style = await page.$eval('h1', el =\u003e el.getAttribute('style')).catch(() =\u003e null);\\n    if (h1Style \u0026\u0026 h1Style.includes('var(--color-')) {\\n      pass('Greeting colour is set via CSS variable inline style');\\n    } else {\\n      fail('Greeting colour should be set via a CSS variable like var(--color-*)', { h1Style });\\n    }\\n\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    fail(`Script error: ${e.message}`);\\n    console.error(e);\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser.close();\\n  }\\n\\n  console.log('\\\\n=== SUMMARY ===');\\n  console.log(`Passed: ${checks.passed.length}`);\\n  console.log(`Failed: ${checks.failed.length}`);\\n  if (checks.failed.length \u003e 0) {\\n    console.log('Failed checks:');\\n    checks.failed.forEach(f =\u003e console.log(` - ${f.msg}: ${JSON.stringify(f.evidence)}`));\\n    process.exit(1);\\n  }\\n})();\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/tmp/verify.js\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_36","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789959622,"id":"chatcmpl-9eeb480f43aa4d5f87aa29d13ad34908","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

